  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Can Tho DAE</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam and five partners will implement Greening Our Rice: Gender-Just, Climate-Smart Rice Production (CSRP) in the Mekong Delta (GoRice), a CAD $8M initiative (2024-2030). The project aims to improve the well-being of rice producers, particularly women and ethnicminorities (EM), through inclusive and CSRP in the Mekong Delta, particularly Tra Vinh, An Giang, and Soc Trang provinces.
GoRice will promote climate-smart practices, enhance women&apos;s and ethnic minorities (EM) empowerment, support low-carbon (LC) rice consumption, and develop carbon Measurement, Reporting, and Verification (MRV) systems and fair carbon projects. GoRice will strengthen collaboration between stakeholders in Vietnam and Canada to enhance cost-benefit sharing mechanisms in carbon projects, green financing, investment, technology transfer, resource mobilization and policy frameworks supporting sustainable CSRP.
GoRice supports the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) and Canada&#x2019;s Indo-Pacific Strategy (IPS), particularly objectives 3, 4, and 5. It aligns with Action Areas 1, 3, and 5 of the Feminist International Assistance Policy (FIAP), with a focus on Action Area 4, and incorporates relevant FIAP indicators into its Performance Measurement Framework (PMF). GoRice complies with the Official Development Assistance Accountability Act, the Comprehensive and Progressive Agreement for Trans-Pacific Partnership (CPTPP), and major international human rights commitments, including the ICCPR and ICESCR, to which Vietnam is a party. GoRice addresses gaps identified through gender equality, human rights, and environmental sustainability analyses, focusing on Article 23 of the Universal Declaration of Human Rights. By promoting sustainable agriculture (Chapter 20), decent work for women andvulnerable groups (Chapter 19), and inclusive economic growth (Chapter 21), GoRice contributes to the CPTPP&#x2019;s goals. GoRice will enhance trade and cooperation between Canada, Vietnam, and other CPTPP countries (Chapter 22), strengthening their reputationsin poverty reduction, gender equality, and environmental sustainability. Acomprehensive Communication and Visibility Action Plan will ensure stakeholder awareness of Canada&#x2019;s support through digital and print media, websites, social media, and campaigns.

The Department of Agriculture and Environment of Can Tho City (Can Tho DAE), one among five partners of GoRice, is a key governmental counterpart at the provincial level, responsible for overseeing agricultural development, natural resource management, and environmental protection. As the lead technical authority in the agriculture sector, CanTho DAE plays a central role in promoting sustainable agricultural practices, supporting climate resilience, and implementing national and local policies related to rice production and environmental sustainability in the Mekong Delta. Within the GoRice project, Can Tho DAE contributes critical technical guidance, policy alignment, and coordination support to ensure effective implementation ofclimate-smart and low-emission rice production models. The department facilitates engagement with local stakeholders, including district authorities, cooperatives, and farmers, and supports the integration of project activities into existing agricultural extension systems. With its strong institutional mandate, technical expertise, and extensive local network, Can Tho DAE is instrumental in scaling sustainable rice production practices, enhancing farmers&#x2019; adaptive capacity, and contributing to the project&#x2019;s overall objectives of reducing greenhouse gas emissions and improving livelihoods for smallholder farmers, particularly women and vulnerable groups.</narrative>
  </description>
