   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Department of Agriculture and Environment of Can Tho City (Can Tho DAE) is a key governmental counterpart at the provincial level, responsible for overseeing agricultural development, natural resource management, and environmental protection. As the lead technical authority in the agriculture sector, Can Tho DAE plays a central role in promoting sustainable agricultural practices, supporting climate resilience, and implementing national and local policies related to rice production and environmental sustainability in the Mekong Delta. Within the GoRice project, Can Tho DAE contributes critical technical guidance, policy alignment, and coordinationsupport to ensure effective implementation of climate-smart and low-emission rice production models. Thedepartment facilitates engagement with local stakeholders, including district authorities, cooperatives, and farmers, and supports the integration of project activities into existing agricultural extension systems. With its strong institutional mandate, technical expertise, and extensive local network, Can Tho DAE is instrumental in scaling sustainable rice production practices, enhancing farmers&#x2019; adaptive capacity, andcontributing to the project&#x2019;s overall objectives of reducing greenhouse gas emissionsand improving livelihoods for smallholder farmers, particularly women and vulnerable groups.</narrative>
